            "stmt_text": "\tret = rspi_request_irq(&pdev->dev, rspi->rx_irq, rspi_irq_mux,\n\t\t\t\t       \"mux\", rspi);",
            "location": "context",
            "explanation": "This IRQ registration statement represents a critical vulnerability point in the SPI-RSPI driver. The rspi_request_irq() call registers an interrupt handler without adequate error handling validation. If the IRQ registration fails, subsequent code may continue assuming the interrupt is properly configured, leading to race conditions, use-after-free scenarios, or denial of service when the driver attempts to use an unregistered or improperly registered interrupt handler. The lack of proper error path handling after this call creates an attack surface for interrupt-related exploits."
